From: PS5_Proton
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: ps5: tell the section cache how many pages a fault may map

A first touch of a large buffer in a demand-mapped section faulted every 16 KiB
(a HashLink game in the earlier emulator experiment (removed): 1,400 faults a second). The fault now passes how many
host pages from the faulting one share its Windows protection exactly, and the
cache maps up to WINE_PS5_SECTION_CLUSTER of them (default 1) in one call, never
past the view or over a cached page.
---
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -5708,8 +5708,17 @@ NTSTATUS virtual_handle_fault( EXCEPTION_RECORD *rec, void *stack )
         PwWineSectionRetry *retry = (PwWineSectionRetry *)&ntdll_get_thread_data()->ps5_section_retry;
         unsigned int access = err == EXCEPTION_EXECUTE_FAULT ? PROT_EXEC :
                               err == EXCEPTION_WRITE_FAULT ? PROT_WRITE : PROT_READ;
+        /* How many host pages from this one share its protection: the cache may map that many in one call (a first touch of
+         * a large buffer would otherwise fault every 16 KiB). */
+        unsigned int run = 1, wanted = __wine_ps5_section_cluster();
+        if (wanted > 1)
+        {
+            BYTE first = get_host_page_vprot( page );
+            while (run < wanted && (char *)page + (run + 1) * (size_t)host_page_size <= (char *)address_space_limit &&
+                   get_host_page_vprot( page + run * (size_t)host_page_size ) == first) run++;
+        }
         int resolved = __wine_ps5_section_fault( (uintptr_t)addr,
-                           get_unix_prot( get_host_page_vprot( page ) ), access, retry );
+                           get_unix_prot( get_host_page_vprot( page ) ), access, retry, run );
         if (resolved > 0) ret = STATUS_SUCCESS;
         else if (resolved < 0)
         {
